    "description": "The inner workings of a fresh workstation PC. Some would also speak of a HEDT, but on the one hand the transitions are fluid and on the other hand the definitions are blurred.  The computer contains an AMD Ryzen Threadripper 7970X with 32 cores, a Gigabyte GeForce RTX 3090 Eagle OC, 64 GiB DDR5 RDIMM RAM (upgrade to 256 GiB planned in the medium term), 1300W power supply unit and more. The computer also offers plenty of space for radiators and data carriers. The graphics card hangs down to the right. It should definitely be supported, which was done later. The interior looks unspectacular, but has a lot to offer. The downward and upward flow direction of the CPU fan is also characteristic. This usually goes to the left and right. Since the Threadripper does not have a graphics unit, a peripheral device with video output is absolutely necessary, such as a graphics card in most cases.",
